      "summaries": {
        "en": "ESM (Evolutionary Scale Modeling) applies large language model techniques to protein sequences, enabling prediction of structure, function, and evolutionary relationships directly from sequence data. Its core innovation is learning protein 'language' from millions of natural sequences without labels, capturing deep evolutionary patterns. Researchers can use ESM for tasks like variant effect prediction, protein design, or as a foundation for fine-tuning on specific biological problems, accelerating discovery in genomics and drug development.",
        "zh": "ESM（进化规模建模）将大型语言模型技术应用于蛋白质序列，能够直接从序列数据预测结构、功能和进化关系。其核心创新在于从数百万天然序列中无监督学习蛋白质的“语言”，捕捉深层的进化模式。研究人员可以利用ESM进行变异效应预测、蛋白质设计，或作为基础模型针对特定生物学问题进行微调，从而加速基因组学和药物开发中的发现。",
        "es": "ESM (Evolutionary Scale Modeling) applies large language model techniques to protein sequences, enabling prediction of structure, function, and evolutionary relationships directly from sequence data. Its core innovation is learning protein 'language' from millions of natural sequences without labels, capturing deep evolutionary patterns. Researchers can use ESM for tasks like variant effect prediction, protein design, or as a foundation for fine-tuning on specific biological problems, accelerating discovery in genomics and drug development.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "esm gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "ESM (Evolutionary Scale Modeling) applies large language model techniques to protein sequences, enabling prediction of structure, function, and evolutionary relationships directly from sequence data. Its core innovation is learning protein 'language' from millions of natural sequences without labels, capturing deep evolutionary patterns. Researchers can use ESM for tasks like variant effect prediction, protein design, or as a foundation for fine-tuning on specific biological problems, accelerating discovery in genomics and drug development.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/Biohub/esm for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
