      "summaries": {
        "en": "Cursor plugins extend the AI-powered code editor with custom commands and integrations. The specification defines a declarative JSON schema for plugin configuration, enabling features like custom slash commands, context providers, and model routing. Developers can create plugins that add specialized workflows, such as automated code reviews or database queries, by defining actions and triggers. To get started, clone the repository, create a plugin manifest, and test it locally with Cursor's developer mode. This modular approach makes it easy to tailor the editor to specific development needs without modifying core functionality.",
        "zh": "Cursor插件规范通过声明式JSON Schema定义配置，支持自定义斜杠命令、上下文提供者和模型路由等特性。开发者可创建插件添加自动代码审查或数据库查询等工作流，仅需定义动作和触发器。使用方式为克隆仓库、创建插件清单并在开发者模式下本地测试。该模块化设计无需修改核心功能即可定制编辑器，降低AI编程工具扩展门槛，便于团队快速构建和共享内部工具，提升协作效率。",
        "es": "Cursor plugins extend the AI-powered code editor with custom commands and integrations. The specification defines a declarative JSON schema for plugin configuration, enabling features like custom slash commands, context providers, and model routing. Developers can create plugins that add specialized workflows, such as automated code reviews or database queries, by defining actions and triggers. To get started, clone the repository, create a plugin manifest, and test it locally with Cursor's developer mode. This modular approach makes it easy to tailor the editor to specific development needs without modifying core functionality.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "plugins gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Cursor plugins extend the AI-powered code editor with custom commands and integrations. The specification defines a declarative JSON schema for plugin configuration, enabling features like custom slash commands, context providers, and model routing. Developers can create plugins that add specialized workflows, such as automated code reviews or database queries, by defining actions and triggers. To get started, clone the repository, create a plugin manifest, and test it locally with Cursor's developer mode. This modular approach makes it easy to tailor the editor to specific development needs without modifying core functionality.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/cursor/plugins for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
