      "summaries": {
        "en": "Stable-WorldModel is a platform for reproducible world model research, addressing the challenge of building predictive models that learn environment dynamics from visual observations. Its core innovation is integrating JEPA (Joint Embedding Predictive Architecture) with model-predictive control, enabling efficient learning of latent representations without reconstructing pixels. This approach reduces computational cost while maintaining planning accuracy. Researchers can use it to benchmark world models, train agents in simulated environments, or extend it for robotics tasks, making it a practical tool for advancing model-based reinforcement learning.",
        "zh": "Stable-WorldModel是一个面向可复现世界模型研究的平台，旨在解决从视觉观测中学习环境动态预测的挑战。其核心创新在于将联合嵌入预测架构（JEPA）与模型预测控制结合，在不重建像素的前提下高效学习潜在表征，显著降低计算成本并保持规划精度。该平台支持世界模型基准测试、模拟环境智能体训练及机器人控制任务扩展，为模型预测控制与强化学习算法研究提供标准化工具，提升研究的可靠性与可复现性。",
        "es": "Stable-WorldModel is a platform for reproducible world model research, addressing the challenge of building predictive models that learn environment dynamics from visual observations. Its core innovation is integrating JEPA (Joint Embedding Predictive Architecture) with model-predictive control, enabling efficient learning of latent representations without reconstructing pixels. This approach reduces computational cost while maintaining planning accuracy. Researchers can use it to benchmark world models, train agents in simulated environments, or extend it for robotics tasks, making it a practical tool for advancing model-based reinforcement learning.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "stable-worldmodel stands out for deep-learning, jepa, and model-predictive-control in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Stable-WorldModel is a platform for reproducible world model research, addressing the challenge of building predictive models that learn environment dynamics from visual observations. Its core innovation is integrating JEPA (Joint Embedding Predictive Architecture) with model-predictive control, enabling efficient learning of latent representations without reconstructing pixels. This approach reduces computational cost while maintaining planning accuracy. Researchers can use it to benchmark world models, train agents in simulated environments, or extend it for robotics tasks, making it a practical tool for advancing model-based reinforcement learning.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/galilai-group/stable-worldmodel for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
